Z||000000||haski||05-17-2000||06:07 PM||||Help ... I'm in the middle of doing an engine conversion and I've encountered a bit of a puzzle. My car is an 84 M24; the donor is (was)a 1987 Buick Park Avenue. The (almost) new engine is a rebuilt 3.8L that has not been modified in any way.<BR>My problem is that the harnesses don't match. To be more specific, the main harness is OK (it, of course, fits its own ECU) but a secondary spur is not. The secondary wiring (I haven't a clue what it's for) on the Buick ends in a big black terminal and is twice the size of the corresponding terminal on the Fiero, which is found under the console about half way between the ECU and the cigarette lighter.<BR>What to do? Anyone have any suggestions? I would appreciate all the help I can get.<BR>I hope to have the car on the road some time in June but anticipate I will have other questions before that. This project is the first of it's kind I have tackled in about 20 years<BR>Cheers,<BR>Haski<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||05-17-2000||10:07 PM||||contact kick hill farms. <A HREF="http://www.kickhill.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kickhill.com</A>  I think. he has all these wires.||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||05-18-2000||12:45 AM||||So there are others suffering from the spaghetti syndrome common to late model engine swaps besides myself.<BR>The only way to identify these wires is to have a schematic that addresses the pin location number where each wire goes into the ECM,then it can be matched up with the corresponding Fiero wire.<BR>I'm trying to get a local dealer to run me a copy of his schematic from his Helm's manual so I don't have to buy a Helms manual for $130.<BR>Helm's Inc. phone number is 313-565-5000,here in Detroit.<BR>Chris west sells a module to bypass the theft deterent device,and/or allow the speedo to work in the automatic cars for $100 or so.<BR>If you have a manual car,the wires have to be connected with the colored wires reversed(yellow to purple,and visa versa).<BR>Or you could just send both harnesses to that place for conversion.||||reg||1
